@* Per-parameter keep-alive: /notes/{id:int} is declared KeepAlive with KeepAliveMax="2", so each
   visited id keeps its OWN instance up to the budget and the least-recently-used one is evicted
   beyond it. The instance stamp changes only when this note was evicted and rebuilt. *@

@inject IBrouter brouter

<h1>Note @Id <span class="muted">(instance #@_instanceStamp)</span></h1>

<div class="card">
    <div class="row">
        <strong>Clicks: @_clicks</strong>
        <button @onclick="@(() => _clicks++)">Click me</button>
    </div>
    <textarea rows="2" style="margin-top: .5rem;" @bind="_draft" placeholder="Draft for note @Id…"></textarea>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <BrouterLink Href="/notes/1" class="btn">Note 1</BrouterLink>
    <BrouterLink Href="/notes/2" class="btn">Note 2</BrouterLink>
    <BrouterLink Href="/notes/3" class="btn">Note 3</BrouterLink>
    <button @onclick="@(() => brouter.ClearKeepAlive())">ClearKeepAlive()</button>
    <button @onclick="@(() => brouter.ClearKeepAlive(includeActive: true))">ClearKeepAlive(includeActive: true)</button>
    <button @onclick="@(() => brouter.ReloadAsync().AsTask())">ReloadAsync()</button>
</div>

<p class="muted">
    Edit notes 1 and 2, then visit note 3: the budget is 2, so the least-recently-used note is
    evicted and returns with a fresh instance stamp and an empty draft. The cache key is the
    template's parameter values, so query-string variations share one instance.
    <code>ClearKeepAlive()</code> disposes every retained page across the app at once - but never the
    visible one. <code>ClearKeepAlive(includeActive: true)</code> rebuilds that one too (same URL, new
    instance stamp, empty draft, no pipeline), and <code>ReloadAsync()</code> does the same while
    re-running guards and loaders.
</p>

@code {
    [Parameter] public int Id { get; set; }

    private int _clicks;
    private string _draft = string.Empty;

    // Monotonic per-instance stamp, so eviction (recreate => new stamp) is visible in the UI.
    private static int _nextStamp;
    private readonly int _instanceStamp = System.Threading.Interlocked.Increment(ref _nextStamp);
}
